"test":{"name":"mp-lobby","kind":"rules","opponent":"Human","rounds":"4","check":"mpLobby","question":"Networked games, the lobby: the host's game gets a join code (6 characters from the settings' alphabet) and a name (the scenario's, the host's to change until it starts: shown as name#code). Players join by the code (typed in any case, with or without the name before it), claim open sides, and cannot take a side someone holds or change what only the host may. The host removes a player, who cannot come back; a device on another version cannot join; a spectator joins to watch. The game cannot start with a side open; once started its name is locked. Each player's list says whose turn it is. A join code is used again once its game is over, under a new epoch (the old game's log is not the new one's). A guest who leaves frees their side; the host leaving ends the game.","rules":"standard"},
